From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] webrtc: drop lifetimebound from a void-returning setter

  error: 'lifetimebound' attribute cannot be applied to a parameter of a
  function that returns void

The attribute ties a parameter's lifetime to the return value, so it is
meaningless on a void setter. clang now rejects it. The constructor parameter
in the same header keeps its attribute, where it is valid.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/third_party/webrtc/api/candidate.h
+++ b/src/third_party/webrtc/api/candidate.h
@@ -107,7 +107,10 @@
   // cricket::LOCAL_PORT_TYPE). The type should really be an enum rather than a
   // string, but until we make that change the lifetime attribute helps us lock
   // things down. See also the `Port` class.
-  void set_type(absl::string_view type ABSL_ATTRIBUTE_LIFETIME_BOUND) {
+  // No ABSL_ATTRIBUTE_LIFETIME_BOUND here: the attribute binds a parameter's
+  // lifetime to the return value, and this function returns void, which clang
+  // now rejects outright.
+  void set_type(absl::string_view type) {
     Assign(type_, type);
   }
 
